// To define a diagnostic, follow the Template format below and add the same name to the DiagnosticCode enum. Every entry states its Category (SPEC 23.3.6.1); Severity defaults to Error. A message takes at most two arguments ({0}, {1}) and no free text; Arguments names each as name:Kind (Number, Enumeration, Boolean, Text or Type), and they become the Reason. Evidence names further facts a report may add to the Reason, all of them or none; alternatives are separated by |, and a report supplies all facts of one alternative. A Label may reference the Reason's facts in order, arguments then evidence.

